{
 "workflow": "fix",
 "name": "fix (keel)",
 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "intake",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "bug report",
   "phase": "bug-report",
   "action": "bug_intake"
  },
  {
   "id": "repro",
   "kind": "agent",
   "name": "bug-repro",
   "agent": "reproducer",
   "model": "default",
   "phase": "bug-repro",
   "markers": [
    "REPRO",
    "LAYER"
   ],
   "instructions": "Work from the symptom (and the reproduction recipe, when there is one) alone. Write the smallest failing test at the lowest layer that shows it, and name it after the bug's id {{data.bug.id}} so keel can run it alone. Never weaken an assertion until something goes red. LAYER: WEB when your test is a web (frontend) test, else API."
  },
  {
   "id": "reproduced",
   "kind": "branch",
   "name": "reproduced",
   "phase": "bug-repro",
   "no": "to_diagnose",
   "when": {
    "marker": "REPRO",
    "equals": "confirmed",
    "step": "repro"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "verify_repro",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "verify red + commit",
   "phase": "bug-repro",
   "action": "verify_red+commit",
   "lock": true
  },
  {
   "id": "gate_r",
   "kind": "gate",
   "name": "gate R",
   "phase": "gate-r",
   "lock": true,
   "choices": {
    "investigate": "hypotheses",
    "reject": "drop_red",
    "stop": "keep_test"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "keep_test",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "stop; the reproducing test stays on the branch",
   "phase": "gate-r",
   "then": "end"
  },
  {
   "id": "drop_red",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "drop the rejected test and reproduce again",
   "phase": "bug-repro",
   "action": "bug_drop_red",
   "then": "repro"
  },
  {
   "id": "hypotheses",
   "kind": "agent",
   "name": "hypotheses",
   "agent": "investigator",
   "model": "default",
   "phase": "bug-investigate",
   "collect": "hypotheses",
   "instructions": "The failing test is committed (the test({{data.bug.id}}) commit). List two to four distinct plausible causes, each one testable on its own. Do not investigate them yet. What earlier fix attempts ruled out (do not list those again): {{data.learned}}\n{{data.evidence_note}}"
  },
  {
   "id": "investigate",
   "kind": "parallel",
   "name": "one investigator per hypothesis",
   "agent": "investigator",
   "model": "default",
   "phase": "bug-investigate",
   "from": "hypotheses",
   "cap": 4,
   "markers": [
    "ROOT-CAUSE"
   ],
   "instructions": "Confirm or kill only the hypothesis in your item, from evidence: the failing test, code, history, logs, read-only queries. Nothing may be edited. ROOT-CAUSE: confirmed means confirmed, not believed. What earlier fix attempts ruled out: {{data.learned}}\n{{data.evidence_note}}"
  },
  {
   "id": "findings",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "collect the findings",
   "phase": "bug-investigate",
   "action": "report"
  },
  {
   "id": "confirmed",
   "kind": "branch",
   "name": "a cause is confirmed",
   "phase": "bug-investigate",
   "no": "escalated",
   "when": {
    "marker": "ROOT-CAUSE",
    "equals": "confirmed",
    "step": "investigate",
    "any": true
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "plan",
   "kind": "agent",
   "name": "fix plan",
   "agent": "investigator",
   "model": "default",
   "phase": "bug-investigate",
   "markers": [
    "E2E"
   ],
   "instructions": "Write the fix plan for Gate F. Start with a \"Root cause:\" line (one or two sentences: it goes into the fix commit's body), then the evidence for it, the files to change, the approach, the risk, one alternative, and whether a regression end-to-end test is needed (E2E: yes when the bug was user-visible across both apps or invisible to a unit test, else no). Fix the cause narrowly; no refactoring.\n{{data.symptoms_note}}\n{{data.evidence_note}}\nThe investigators' answers:\n{{data.report}}"
  },
  {
   "id": "plan_report",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "plan for gate F",
   "phase": "bug-investigate",
   "action": "report+bug_plan"
  },
  {
   "id": "gate_f",
   "kind": "gate",
   "name": "gate F",
   "phase": "gate-f",
   "lock": true,
   "choices": {
    "fix": "fix",
    "investigate": "hypotheses",
    "feature": "hand_feature",
    "reject": "plan"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "hand_feature",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "start the feature flow with the evidence",
   "phase": "gate-f",
   "action": "start_flow",
   "flow": "feature",
   "seed": {
    "title": "$title",
    "evidence": "$data.report"
   },
   "then": "end"
  },
  {
   "id": "fix",
   "kind": "agent",
   "name": "bug-fix",
   "agent": "implementer",
   "model": "default",
   "phase": "bug-fix",
   "instructions": "Change the cause, never the test (tests are frozen in this phase). Touch only the files the approved plan names and explain any extra one. Put the root cause in your summary. The approved plan:\n{{data.report}}"
  },
  {
   "id": "verify_fix",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "verify + commit",
   "phase": "bug-fix",
   "action": "verify_green+commit",
   "back": "hypotheses",
   "lock": true,
   "rounds": 1,
   "after_rounds": "reset"
  },
  {
   "id": "e2e_needed",
   "kind": "branch",
   "name": "regression e2e needed",
   "phase": "bug-fix",
   "no": "ship_plan",
   "when": {
    "marker": "E2E",
    "equals": "yes",
    "step": [
     "intake",
     "plan"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "e2e",
   "kind": "agent",
   "name": "regression e2e",
   "agent": "e2e-author",
   "model": "default",
   "phase": "e2e",
   "markers": [
    "E2E-RESULT"
   ],
   "instructions": "Write one end-to-end test for the journey that used to break, run it, and keep it only if it adds cover the reproducing test does not."
  },
  {
   "id": "e2e_commit",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "commit e2e",
   "phase": "e2e",
   "action": "commit"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_plan",
   "kind": "gate",
   "name": "which ship steps run",
   "phase": "ship",
   "lock": true,
   "skip_menu": true,
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_doc_updates",
   "kind": "agent",
   "name": "docs the change makes wrong",
   "agent": "implementer",
   "model": "default",
   "phase": "close",
   "instructions": "This step is about the project's own docs, not code and not keel's knowledge base. Read the branch diff against the base branch, then the README, the CHANGELOG (when the project keeps one), the API docs (an OpenAPI description, docs/api, pages for the routes this branch adds or changes) and the user guide pages. Edit only what this change makes wrong or incomplete: a new or changed route, flag, config key, command or behaviour a reader would miss. A project with a CHANGELOG gets one entry under its unreleased heading. Touch no code, no test, no spec and nothing in the knowledge base; keep each edit small. When nothing is wrong, change nothing and say so. End with one line per file you changed and why: the final review shows it.",
   "skippable": "optional",
   "group": "doc_updates",
   "keep": true,
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_doc_updates_commit",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "commit the doc edits",
   "phase": "close",
   "action": "commit",
   "skippable": "optional",
   "group": "doc_updates",
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_verify_fix",
   "kind": "agent",
   "name": "fix what the checks found",
   "agent": "implementer",
   "model": "default",
   "phase": "review-fix",
   "retry_only": true,
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_verify_fix_commit",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "commit the fix",
   "phase": "review-fix",
   "action": "commit",
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_verify",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "verify fast + module",
   "phase": "ship",
   "action": "verify_fast+verify_module",
   "lock": true,
   "rounds": 2,
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_lint",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "static checks",
   "phase": "ship",
   "action": "verify_lint",
   "soft": true,
   "skippable": "optional",
   "group": "lint",
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_ci",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "the project's CI jobs on CI's versions",
   "phase": "ship",
   "action": "ci_pipeline",
   "soft": true,
   "skippable": "optional",
   "group": "ci",
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_release",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "verify release",
   "phase": "ship",
   "action": "verify_release",
   "rounds": 2,
   "skippable": "deferred",
   "group": "release",
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_cover_measure",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "measure coverage",
   "phase": "coverage-fix",
   "action": "verify_coverage",
   "lock": true,
   "soft": true,
   "skippable": "deferred",
   "group": "cover",
   "included_from": "ship/cover"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_cover_measured",
   "kind": "branch",
   "name": "the coverage command failed",
   "phase": "coverage-fix",
   "no": "ship_cover_needs_work",
   "when": {
    "data": "coverage_error"
   },
   "skippable": "deferred",
   "group": "cover",
   "included_from": "ship/cover"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_cover_measure_failed",
   "kind": "gate",
   "name": "coverage could not be measured",
   "phase": "coverage-fix",
   "when": {
    "data": "coverage_error"
   },
   "skippable": "deferred",
   "group": "cover",
   "choices": {
    "try_again": "ship_cover_measure",
    "go_on": "ship_cover_report"
   },
   "included_from": "ship/cover"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_cover_needs_work",
   "kind": "branch",
   "name": "coverage fails",
   "phase": "coverage-fix",
   "no": "ship_cover_report",
   "when": {
    "marker": "RESULT",
    "step": "ship_cover_measure",
    "equals": "fail"
   },
   "skippable": "deferred",
   "group": "cover",
   "included_from": "ship/cover"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_cover_no_reports",
   "kind": "gate",
   "name": "cover needs coverage.reports",
   "phase": "coverage-fix",
   "when": {
    "data": "coverage_no_reports"
   },
   "skippable": "deferred",
   "group": "cover",
   "choices": {
    "go_on": "ship_cover_report",
    "stop": "end"
   },
   "included_from": "ship/cover"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_cover_decide",
   "kind": "gate",
   "name": "decide test / delete / accept",
   "phase": "coverage-fix",
   "lock": true,
   "for_each": "coverage_groups",
   "per_item": true,
   "skippable": "deferred",
   "group": "cover",
   "choices": [
    "test",
    "delete",
    "accept"
   ],
   "on_skip": {
    "choice": "accept",
    "record": "coverage_accepted"
   },
   "included_from": "ship/cover"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_cover_write",
   "kind": "agent",
   "name": "cover the group: write the test, or delete the unreachable lines",
   "agent": "test-author",
   "model": "default",
   "phase": "coverage-fix",
   "per_item": true,
   "skippable": "deferred",
   "group": "cover",
   "included_from": "ship/cover"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_cover_review",
   "kind": "agent",
   "name": "review the coverage test: assertions lens",
   "agent": "lens-reviewer",
   "model": "default",
   "phase": "coverage-fix",
   "back": "ship_cover_write",
   "lock": true,
   "per_item": true,
   "instructions": "When the item's decision is delete: is the deleted code really unreachable? Look for callers, routes, reflection, configuration, scheduled jobs and event handlers that reach it; if anything can, that is blocking.",
   "rounds": 2,
   "skippable": "deferred",
   "group": "cover",
   "included_from": "ship/cover"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_cover_commit",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "coverage commit",
   "phase": "coverage-fix",
   "action": "commit",
   "back": "ship_cover_write",
   "lock": true,
   "per_item": true,
   "skippable": "deferred",
   "group": "cover",
   "included_from": "ship/cover"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_cover_remeasure",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "measure again",
   "phase": "coverage-fix",
   "action": "verify_coverage",
   "lock": true,
   "soft": true,
   "skippable": "deferred",
   "group": "cover",
   "included_from": "ship/cover"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_cover_covered",
   "kind": "branch",
   "name": "coverage passes",
   "phase": "coverage-fix",
   "no": "ship_cover_decide",
   "when": {
    "marker": "RESULT",
    "step": "ship_cover_remeasure",
    "equals": "pass"
   },
   "rounds": 2,
   "skippable": "deferred",
   "group": "cover",
   "included_from": "ship/cover"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_cover_report",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "coverage verdict",
   "phase": "coverage-fix",
   "action": "coverage_report",
   "skippable": "deferred",
   "group": "cover",
   "included_from": "ship/cover"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_deps",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "verify deps",
   "phase": "ship",
   "action": "verify_deps",
   "skippable": "deferred",
   "group": "deps",
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_audit",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "audit",
   "phase": "ship",
   "action": "audit",
   "lock": true,
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_trace",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "trace --strict",
   "phase": "ship",
   "action": "trace_strict",
   "lock": true,
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_lenses",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "review lenses",
   "phase": "ship",
   "action": "review_lenses",
   "skippable": "optional",
   "group": "reviewers",
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_review",
   "kind": "parallel",
   "name": "ship review, one lens each",
   "agent": "lens-reviewer",
   "model": "default",
   "phase": "ship",
   "from": "review_lenses",
   "rounds": 2,
   "redo": "ship_verify",
   "skippable": "optional",
   "group": "reviewers",
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_spec_walk",
   "kind": "agent",
   "name": "walk the diff against the spec: name behaviour no criterion asks for",
   "agent": "lens-reviewer",
   "model": "default",
   "phase": "ship",
   "when": {
    "state": "spec"
   },
   "rounds": 2,
   "redo": "ship_verify",
   "skippable": "optional",
   "group": "spec_walk",
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_final_review",
   "kind": "gate",
   "name": "final review",
   "phase": "final-review",
   "back": "ship_verify_fix",
   "lock": true,
   "report": "verdicts",
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_memory_plan",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "is the knowledge base stale?",
   "phase": "memory",
   "action": "memory_plan",
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_memory_gate",
   "kind": "gate",
   "name": "update the knowledge base?",
   "phase": "memory",
   "when": {
    "data": "memory_plan.ask",
    "equals": "yes"
   },
   "choices": {
    "update": "ship_memory",
    "skip": "ship_memory_skip"
   },
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_memory_skip",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "skip the knowledge update",
   "phase": "memory",
   "action": "memory_skip",
   "when": {
    "data": "memory_plan.ask",
    "equals": "yes"
   },
   "then": "ship_memory_check",
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_memory",
   "kind": "agent",
   "name": "knowledge update",
   "agent": "librarian",
   "model": "default",
   "phase": "memory",
   "when": {
    "data": "memory_plan.run",
    "equals": "yes"
   },
   "instructions": "Update only these sections, and in them only the claims that cite the files listed (they changed since the last knowledge check). Re-read those files, fix or remove what is no longer true, add what this branch makes worth knowing, and keep every other line as it is. A section listed as not written yet is written from the code.\n{{data.memory_plan.text}}",
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_memory_check",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "knowledge check",
   "phase": "memory",
   "action": "knowledge_check",
   "when": {
    "data": "memory_plan.check",
    "equals": "yes"
   },
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_memory_commit",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "commit memory",
   "phase": "memory",
   "action": "commit",
   "when": {
    "data": "memory_plan.run",
    "equals": "yes"
   },
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_pr",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "PR body",
   "phase": "close",
   "action": "pr",
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_pr_gate",
   "kind": "gate",
   "name": "open the PR",
   "phase": "close",
   "lock": true,
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "ship_open_pr",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "open the PR (never pushes)",
   "phase": "close",
   "action": "open_pr",
   "included_from": "ship"
  },
  {
   "id": "finish",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "done",
   "phase": "close",
   "then": "end"
  },
  {
   "id": "escalated",
   "kind": "branch",
   "name": "model already escalated",
   "phase": "bug-investigate",
   "no": "escalate",
   "when": {
    "marker": "ESCALATED",
    "equals": "yes",
    "step": "escalate"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "to_diagnose",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "hand to diagnose",
   "phase": "bug-investigate",
   "action": "start_flow",
   "flow": "diagnose",
   "seed": {
    "title": "$title",
    "symptoms": [
     "$request"
    ],
    "evidence": "$data.report"
   },
   "then": "end"
  },
  {
   "id": "escalate",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "escalate the investigator's model once",
   "agent": "investigator",
   "phase": "bug-investigate",
   "action": "escalate_model",
   "then": "investigate"
  },
  {
   "id": "reset",
   "kind": "code",
   "name": "reset and investigate again",
   "phase": "reset",
   "action": "bug_reset",
   "then": "hypotheses"
  }
 ],
 "expect": {
  "main": [
   "intake",
   "repro",
   "reproduced",
   "verify_repro",
   "gate_r",
   "hypotheses",
   "investigate",
   "findings",
   "confirmed",
   "plan",
   "plan_report",
   "gate_f",
   "fix",
   "verify_fix",
   "e2e_needed",
   "e2e",
   "e2e_commit",
   "ship_plan",
   "ship_doc_updates",
   "ship_doc_updates_commit",
   "ship_verify_fix",
   "ship_verify_fix_commit",
   "ship_verify",
   "ship_lint",
   "ship_ci",
   "ship_release",
   "ship_cover_measure",
   "ship_cover_measured",
   "ship_cover_measure_failed",
   "ship_cover_needs_work",
   "ship_cover_no_reports",
   "ship_cover_decide",
   "ship_cover_write",
   "ship_cover_review",
   "ship_cover_commit",
   "ship_cover_remeasure",
   "ship_cover_covered",
   "ship_cover_report",
   "ship_deps",
   "ship_audit",
   "ship_trace",
   "ship_lenses",
   "ship_review",
   "ship_spec_walk",
   "ship_final_review",
   "ship_memory_plan",
   "ship_memory_gate",
   "ship_memory",
   "ship_memory_check",
   "ship_memory_commit",
   "ship_pr",
   "ship_pr_gate",
   "ship_open_pr",
   "finish"
  ],
  "sections": [
   {
    "kind": "phase",
    "phase": "bug-report",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "step": "intake",
      "side": []
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "kind": "phase",
    "phase": "bug-repro",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "step": "repro",
      "side": []
     },
     {
      "if": "reproduced",
      "cond": "bug-repro says REPRO = confirmed",
      "side": [],
      "yes": "go",
      "no": {
       "nodes": [
        {
         "step": "to_diagnose",
         "side": []
        }
       ],
       "side": true
      }
     },
     {
      "step": "verify_repro",
      "side": []
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "kind": "phase",
    "phase": "gate-r",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "step": "gate_r",
      "side": [
       "keep_test",
       "drop_red"
      ]
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "kind": "phase",
    "phase": "bug-investigate",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "step": "hypotheses",
      "side": []
     },
     {
      "step": "investigate",
      "side": []
     },
     {
      "step": "findings",
      "side": []
     },
     {
      "if": "confirmed",
      "cond": "one investigator per hypothesis (any of them) says ROOT-CAUSE = confirmed",
      "side": [],
      "yes": "go",
      "no": {
       "nodes": [
        {
         "step": "escalated",
